    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (74.60) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Kyle Tucker** remains a foundational anchor despite a neutral platoon stance against Gasser, as his raw talent profile thrives against favorable SP_xERA matchups. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from a dynamic platoon advantage and a premium #2 spot in the order, positioning him to capitalize on the 4.34 xERA of Holmes. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) also presents an elite start; his placement at the leadoff spot, paired with wind conditions blowing out and an impressive 0.397 xwOBA, makes him a premier target for maximizing our run production.\n\nThe decision to bench **Nolan Schanuel** (41.65) was the most difficult call of the morning, as his efficiency remained respectable. However, **Nolan Schanuel** fell short of the threshold because he is facing a high-caliber arm in Eovaldi (3.19 xERA), which suppressed his SP Skill adjustment enough to justify leaving him on the bench in favor of higher-efficiency hitters like **Andy Pages** (68.07). Caution is advised with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73), whose score is heavily depressed by a brutal matchup against Skenes; while his talent floor is high, his limited efficiency today suggests he is a marginal play. Furthermore, keep a close watch on **Josh Jung**, whose status remains pending; if he is not confirmed in the #2 hole as assumed, his score may see volatility. Finally, we must navigate the total loss of **Gunnar Henderson** due to a confirmed rainout, while **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth as we chase points in the scarce stolen base category.",
